Carafe bench: svcGetInfo(ThreadTickCount) reports the CPU time of another thread for all cores.
Eden answered 0 unless the handle was the calling thread, so Autorun's [THREADS] lines read 0.00 cores and its
sampling profiler never picked a thread. The time accumulated at the thread's last context switch is returned.
GPL-3.0-or-later, as the file it changes.

--- a/src/core/hle/kernel/svc/svc_info.cpp
+++ b/src/core/hle/kernel/svc/svc_info.cpp
@@ -224,6 +224,8 @@
             out_ticks = thread_ticks + (core_timing.GetClockTicks() - prev_ctx_ticks);
         } else if (same_thread && info_sub_id == system.Kernel().CurrentPhysicalCoreIndex()) {
             out_ticks = core_timing.GetClockTicks() - prev_ctx_ticks;
+        } else if (!same_thread && info_sub_id == 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF) {
+            out_ticks = static_cast<u64>(thread->GetCpuTime());
         }
 
         *result = out_ticks;
